execution/feed.js canonicalises EVERY price and quantity on every book
level and every print through fromNumberLexeme. The sampled minute after
FIX-111 on d58a8012: fromNumberLexeme 7% . parseLexemes 3% . normalize 3%
of a saturated main thread.

The function is pure - the same lexeme always canonicalises to the same
string - so it now carries a bounded memo exactly like parseDecimal's
(65,536 entries, cleared when full). A hit returns the byte-identical
string the two regexes, BigInt, format and parse would have produced; a
malformed lexeme throws before the store and is never remembered.
Fenced (5,000 random lexemes, hit == miss). judge-differential green.

